A minimal agent is an **LLM–tool–observation loop**:

1. Send the user request and tool schemas to the LLM.
2. If the LLM requests a tool, validate and execute it.
3. Append the tool result to the conversation.
4. Call the LLM again.
5. Stop when it calls `finish`—or, as a fallback, when it returns no tool calls.

The article’s first milestone uses exactly two tools: `execute_code` and `finish`. The model decides *what* to do; the Python harness decides *how* to execute it.  
Source: [Agents Zero to Hero #1](https://nik-hil.hashnode.dev/agents-zero-to-hero-1-building-an-ai-agent-from-scratch-with-tool-calling)

